cubie-a7z-fanctl for Debian 13
============================
The service is not enabled or started on initial installation. The default
configuration targets Cubie A7Z: hwmon name pwmfan, CPU temperature zones
0 and 3, and fallback disabled.

Configuration: /etc/cubie-a7z-fanctl/config.toml
Validate and enable the service:
  sudo cubie-a7z-fanctl --check-config
  sudo systemctl enable --now cubie-a7z-fanctl
Restart the service after editing its configuration.

Configuration is managed as a Debian conffile; upgrades preserve administrator
changes. Upgrades restart a running service and leave a stopped service stopped.
Remove stops the service and retains configuration; purge also removes
configuration and service enablement state.

See README.md (possibly compressed) for build instructions, configuration and
troubleshooting, and cubie-a7z-fanctl(8) for command-line details.
